7. Local Triad and Empty Named-Policy Inventory

The single private local classifier enforces exactly:
SELECTIVE -> reason None, policy None.
PROOF_BASED_FULL_CLOSURE -> reason AFFECTED_CLOSURE_EQUALS_ALL_RECOMPUTABLE_WORK, policy None.
NAMED_POLICY -> reason FAIL_CLOSED_POLICY_REQUIRES_FULL_RECONSTRUCTION and an accepted policy ID.

The accepted named-policy inventory is the exact empty tuple. No nonempty
policy ID is accepted. The old magic policy and legacy reason literals are
absent from current runtime semantics. Arbitrary scope, reason, policy, proof
reason with non-null policy, named-policy reason with null or unapproved policy,
and SELECTIVE with whole-run fields all fail closed.

8. Binding-Projector Responsibility Audit

The binding projector validates only the exact baseline/observed source pair,
stable topology/node/cell witness, local triad, canonical identity, exact
parents and traces, and zero-authority material. It calls the local triad
classifier and does not call the aggregate closure classifier. One binding
artifact does not claim or prove multi-binding full closure.

9. Independent Aggregate Full-Closure Proof Audit

The aggregate proof accepts only a validated baseline execution bundle and
canonical validated binding artifacts. It accepts no caller-precomputed node,
cell, artifact, closure inventory, boolean, or PASS label. It derives direct
work rows from binding payloads, baseline recomputable rows from cell inputs,
queue entries/artifacts, cell results/result artifacts and the report artifact,
and parent-closed execution rows from topology and cell-projection laws.

The classifier returns only STRICT_SUBSET, FULL_CLOSURE, or INVALID. The
context builder and structural, contextual, complete-bundle, and public-run
validators all call the same aggregate proof and require exact rederived
ordered material. Positive full closure is built from actual baseline objects
and public source/binding evidence. Strict-subset whole-run, full-closure
SELECTIVE, forged, missing, foreign, reordered, ambiguous, and unsupported
material fail closed.

10. Public Run and Complete-Bundle Audit

The public run preserves the historical context=None call law. For a non-null
context it performs structural validation, contextual source/basis validation,
local proof-class validation, and independently rederived FULL_CLOSURE before
the internal admission/queue/budget executor. It validates the complete
28-field result bundle. A SELECTIVE context on the public whole-run seam returns
(None, FAIL_CLOSED) before runtime admission and does not raise through the
public seam.

11. Activation-Witness and Stage-D Parent-Closure Audit

The support-closure helper derives ancestors from exact parent refs, includes
baseline queue/result/report activation witnesses, coalesces duplicate-equal
support, rejects duplicate-unequal, missing, foreign, inverted, cyclic and
unknown-parent support, and emits deterministic parent-before-child order with
lexical artifact-ID tie-break. Stage-D overlap is admitted only for
canonical-byte-equal artifacts. Stable root and child witnesses are rederived
from exact public baseline material.

12. Identity, Trace, Report, and Causal Propagation Audit

The proof reason and Python None policy are present in exact binding payload
material and affect binding identity. Context identity rebuild is exact.
Binding/context IDs enter only their exact queue and cell-input lineage. The
current trace is bound into the runtime report; report-artifact parent/trace
material and causal rows bind the current queue, result, report and trace
family. No direct field is claimed where the contract proves only
cryptographic or parent/trace lineage.

